From 70764b7563cec12fd9bbd6fa0970d55cf6f410cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:11:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ci): publish with JFrog CLI, attest artifacts and
 refresh docker images

- docker-build-push: record the image in a JFrog build-info
  (jf rt build-docker-create), embed max-mode provenance next to the BuildKit
  SBOM, attest with an oci:// subject so setup-jfrog-cli attaches the
  attestation to the image in Artifactory as evidence.
- docker-build-push: add 'refresh' mode to rebuild a released tag with fresh
  base images and no cache and overwrite its image tag, optionally moving the
  floating and latest tags.
- maven/gradle publish: deploy with 'jf mvn' / 'jf gradle artifactoryPublish'
  through OIDC, deploy the CycloneDX SBOM, publish build-info.
- new jfrog-publish-attest action: publish build-info, attest every artifact of
  the build-info (provenance + SBOM) and record them as JFrog evidence.
- setup-jfrog-cli v5.3.5 with pinned JFrog CLI 2.133.0, actions pinned by SHA.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015o1T6BSTNddWikJrEPdP4m
