+### JFrog CLI publishing, SBOMs and attestations
+
+The Maven and Gradle publish workflows deploy with the JFrog CLI (`jf mvn deploy` / `jf gradle artifactoryPublish`)
+using GitHub OIDC (`jfrog/setup-jfrog-cli`, pinned JFrog CLI version), then the
+[`jfrog-publish-attest`](.github/actions/jfrog-publish-attest/action.yaml) action:
+
+1. adds git and environment details and publishes the build-info (`jf rt build-publish`);
+2. lists every artifact of the build-info (AQL) and creates a GitHub build-provenance attestation and a
+   CycloneDX SBOM attestation for all of them (subject names are the Artifactory paths);
+3. attaches both attestations to the deployed artifacts as JFrog evidence (`jf evd create --sigstore-bundle`).
+
+The CycloneDX SBOM is deployed next to the artifacts (Maven: attached by `cyclonedx-maven-plugin`; Gradle:
+uploaded as `<name>-<version>-cyclonedx.json`) and is part of the build-info. Callers must grant
+`id-token: write` and `attestations: write` (and `contents: write` for dependency submission). Attestations can be verified with `gh attestation verify <file> --repo <owner>/<repo>`.
+
+New inputs: `deploy-repo`, `resolve-repo` (empty: keep the build's own repositories), `sbom-path`,
+`sbom-task` (Gradle), `evidence`. `maven-repo-id` is deprecated and ignored.
 
 ### Maven Snapshot Publish to Repository
 
-This workflow publishes a Maven snapshot to a JFROG Maven repository. It assumes that the `deploy` goal is configured to deploy the artifacts to a repository.
-It also assumes that the repository URL is configured in the `pom.xml` file, also that the server id is the same as the one supplied in the `maven-repo-id` input.
+This workflow publishes a Maven snapshot to a JFrog Maven repository with `jf mvn deploy` (see [JFrog CLI publishing](#jfrog-cli-publishing-sboms-and-attestations)).
+The deployment repository is given with `deploy-repo` (default `ecodex-snapshots`); `distributionManagement` credentials are not needed.
 
